: "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01RJ4hSRM7iYfhNXyzm164WP", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 378068, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I upgraded fastjson from 2.8.0 to 2.9.4 to fix CVE-2026-31337 and opened pull request #101 against main, with alex requested as reviewer.\n\n- **Branch:** `fix/upgrade-fastjson-cve-2026-31337`, created from main. The only change is `requirements.txt`, which now pins `fastjson==2.9.4`. `requests` is unchanged.\n- **Version choice:** The advisory lists 2.9.4 and 3.1.0 as fixed versions. I picked 2.9.4 to stay on the 2.x line, since 3.1.0 is a major-version jump. The PR description says so.\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` on commit `c8b8ab7878` passed.\n- **Not done:** I did not merge. Merging into main needs approval from a code owner, so the PR is waiting on that.\n- **Not included:** I left `CHANGELOG.md` alone. Its \"Unreleased\" section is empty, so a changelog entry could go in before merge if the team wants one.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I'll start by checking the advisory and finding where fastjson is pinned.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01Y2ZtrZxbj6cKKmQWGTioac", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"id": "CVE-2026-31337"}, "name": "get_advisory", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01VZM6UYM7WAXW1s3GAfXsLS", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_files", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The advisory says 2.8.0 is affected and the fix is in 2.9.4. Next I'll read the requirements file and the changelog.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01KTZS5j5yZjxFrUBwYKNqa3", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "requirements.txt"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01MMibeyuSGsbwnB9cBJ7EYF", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "CHANGELOG.md"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01SZnxwnb2LmBJ9UeCEx7nxz", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/upgrade-fastjson-cve-2026-31337", "from_ref": "main"}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The branch is created. I'll pin fastjson to 2.9.4, the minimal fixed version on the 2.x line, and leave the other pin unchanged.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_014tnNPrcjmH2xAh3TnjdrPB", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/upgrade-fastjson-cve-2026-31337", "message": "Upgrade fastjson 2.8.0 -> 2.9.4 to fix CVE-2026-31337", "files": [{"path": "requirements.txt", "content": "fastjson==2.9.4\nrequests==2.32.3\n"}]}, "name": "commit_changes", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_0119bBDGhc2kf8nWYbirSqjP", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"ref": "fix/upgrade-fastjson-cve-2026-31337", "idempotency_key": "fastjson-cve-2026-31337-c8b8ab7878"}, "name": "trigger_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01SfmQ5Er2mXTChH5npFwdcj", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"run_id": "ci-0001"}, "name": "wait_for_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "CI passed on the branch. Now I'll open the pull request against main with alex as reviewer.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01RJ4hSRM7iYfhNXyzm164WP", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/upgrade-fastjson-cve-2026-31337", "base": "main", "title": "Upgrade fastjson 2.8.0 -> 2.9.4 to fix CVE-2026-31337", "body": "## Summary\nBumps fastjson from 2.8.0 to 2.9.4 in `requirements.txt`.\n\nCVE-2026-31337 (high): unbounded recursion when parsing deeply nested arrays. Affects `<2.9.4` and `>=3.0.0 <3.1.0`. Fixed in 2.9.4 and 3.1.0.\n\nThis PR picks 2.9.4 to stay on the 2.x line. Moving to 3.1.0 would be a major-version change and is not part of this fix.\n\n## Testing\n- CI run `ci-0001` on commit `c8b8ab7878`: passed.\n", "reviewers": ["alex"]}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I upgraded fastjson from 2.8.0 to 2.9.4 to fix CVE-2026-31337 and opened pull request #101 against main, with alex requested as reviewer.\n\n- **Branch:** `fix/upgrade-fastjson-cve-2026-31337`, created from main. The only change is `requirements.txt`, which now pins `fastjson==2.9.4`. `requests` is unchanged.\n- **Version choice:** The advisory lists 2.9.4 and 3.1.0 as fixed versions. I picked 2.9.4 to stay on the 2.x line, since 3.1.0 is a major-version jump. The PR description says so.\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` on commit `c8b8ab7878` passed.\n- **Not done:** I did not merge. Merging into main needs approval from a code owner, so the PR is waiting on that.\n- **Not included:** I left `CHANGELOG.md` alone. Its \"Unreleased\" section is empty, so a changelog entry could go in before merge if the team wants one.", "type": "text"}]}]}